Heath G. Goebel writes:
>Do most gun-owners on this list leave their gun at home,
>persumably for at home protection? Or do you keep your gun
>on your person?
>
>I expect that most would keep it on their person,
>except where prohibited by law, in order to afford
>both protection at home and on the streets.

As a UK citizen, I have little choice but to leave my guns (four pistols of
various types) in a locked safe at home, except when I go shooting. 
However, if it were legal to carry them for self-protection, I would not
bother to do so, nor even keep a loaded gun by the bed at night.  I live in
a peaceful area of a peaceful town, and my home has only been burgled once
(I was out of the country at the time).  In fact, I have never been
anywhere (including, for example, London, Amsterdam, New York, San
Francisco, and Las Vegas) where I have felt in need of a handy weapon.

On the other hand, if I were in a place where concealed-carry permits were
routinely available, I would get one, and at least part of the reason I
took up shooting in the first place was the possibility that it might one
day be a useful skill to have.

